{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovTr_physical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovTr_physical","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovNormalized.lean#L108-L129","doc":"**The whole statement in one place.** At the weight the peel forces — `w = (1, q²)`, whose\ntotal is `1 + q²` — the normalised trace is a Markov trace with parameter `q³ · (1+q²)⁻¹`, i.e.\nconvention D's `z = q³/(q²+1)`.\n\nThe three conclusions are the three axioms; the fourth is the parameter's characterisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovParam_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovParam_unique","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovNormalized.lean#L102-L106","doc":"That equation pins the scalar: no other `z` satisfies it once `1 + q²` is invertible. So\n\"the Markov parameter is `q³/(q²+1)`\" is a determination, not a choice of representative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovParam_eq_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovParam_eq_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovNormalized.lean#L96-L100","doc":"**The normalised peel scalar is `q³·(1+q²)⁻¹`.** Stated division-free: it is the unique\nsolution of `ẑ · (q² + 1) = q³`, which is convention D's `z = q³/(q² + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovTr_peel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovTr_peel","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovNormalized.lean#L83-L92","doc":"**Axiom 3 — the peel, normalised.** The scalar picks up one factor of `wi`: if the\nunnormalised peel scalar is `z`, the normalised one is `z · wi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovTr_mul_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovTr_mul_comm","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovNormalized.lean#L77-L81","doc":"**Axiom 2 — cyclicity.** Inherited from `qTrace_mul_comm`: the normalisation is a scalar. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovTr_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovTr_one","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovNormalized.lean#L71-L75","doc":"**Axiom 1 — normalisation.** `tr̂(1) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovTr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovTr","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovNormalized.lean#L65-L69","doc":"**The normalised trace** `tr̂(x) = wi^{m+1} · tr_w(x)`, where `wi` is the inverse of the\ntotal weight `∑ₖ w k`, carried explicitly rather than as a field division. ","signatureChunk":0}]}